{
  "slug": "peer-channel",
  "name": "Peer Channel",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Peer-to-peer messaging between Claude Code sessions on the same machine.",
  "longDescription": "A stdio MCP server (`channel.js`, Node.js 20 or later) that lets Claude Code sessions on one machine message each other. Each session's channel claims a name with a lockfile under `~/.peer-channel/sessions/<name>.lock`, listens on the Unix socket `<name>.sock` next to it, and talks to peers directly over `AF_UNIX` with NDJSON: no daemon, no Docker, no TCP port. Needs Claude Code 2.1.80 or later with a claude.ai login, since channels are a research preview. MIT, version 0.3.0.",
